\author{utensil}
\date{2026-08-12}

\p{These notes accompany the Lean project
\href{https://github.com/utensil/connes-rigidity}{connes-rigidity}. Zhou's
Theorem A constructs two countable groups that are ICC and have property (T),
whose tracial group factors are isomorphic although the groups themselves are
not. The formalization therefore has one construction stage and four logically
separate certificate lanes: factor equivalence, property (T), ICC, and group
nonisomorphism. The final theorem merely assembles those four endpoints.}

\p{The diagram is a map of both the proof and the notes. Solid arrows are
internal Lean developments. The dashed arrow is the sole substantive
mathematical input left external: the Ershov--Jaikin-Zapirain--Kassabov
property-(T) theorem for #{\mathrm{EL}_3(\mathbb F_2[t])}. Each lane uses a
separate port at the construction and theorem nodes.}

